---
description: Route non-trivial work through the agent-skills lifecycle in .cursor/skills/
alwaysApply: true
---

Before starting non-trivial technical work:

1. Route via `.cursor/skills/using-agent-skills/SKILL.md` — it maps the task to the right
   skill(s) across Define → Plan → Build → Verify → Review → Ship.
2. Read and follow the matching skill(s) under `.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` in full,
   not just the frontmatter description.
3. Open `.cursor/references/<name>.md` when a skill links to a `references/*.md`
   checklist, and `.cursor/agents/<name>.md` when it points to a persona.
4. Prefer these project skills over guessing an approach — you don't need the user to say
   "read the skill" each time; check for an applicable one first.

For the phase-by-phase entry points (`/spec /plan /build /test /review /code-simplify
/webperf /ship`), see the command skills of the same name in `.cursor/skills/`.
